T2/T3/T4 NLL 2.35/3.10/2.65/0.92; tangent_successor_residual: T1/T2/T3/T4 NLL 4.00/3.17/1.67/0.29 -> {\"l1_br\": {\"n_eval\": 57439, \"reproduction\": {\"absolute_difference\": 0.006023781731602222, \"ndcg_absolute_difference\": 0.0034505417660031304, \"reported_ndcg@10\": 0.021673569339540715, \"reported_test_recall@10\": 0.04068664\n  [E8] OBSERVED | measured first-level capacity ceiling on the frozen Stage1 vectors: share of canonical pairs whose anchor and target share one of K clusters is K=16 0.3106 (negative 0.1352), K=32 0.2164 (negative 0.0715), K=64 0.1547 (negative 0.0376), K=256 0.0822 (negative 0.0129); a small K keeps behavioural neighbours together far more often in absolute terms, which is what width-20 prefix survival depends on -> {\"cohort_profile_signal\": {\"cohorts\": 64, \"definition\": \"the profile of an item is the distribution of its train-only predecessors over successor-cohorts; the positive/negative rates use the same 52,855 held-out valid pa\n  [E9] OBSERVED | measured train-only cohort-profile signal: a positive shares a successor cohort with its anchor 0.9291 of the time against 0.8871 for the fixed negatives, and the positive's profile overlap exceeds every one of its ten negatives for 0.5898 of pairs; profile entropy averages 1.65 nats over 7.5 cohorts per item, so the profile is not degenerate -> {\"cohort_profile_signal\": {\"cohorts\": 64, \"definition\": \"the profile of an item is the distribution of its train-only predecessors over successor-cohorts; the positive/negative rates use the same 52,855 held-out valid pa\n  [E10] OK | measured train-only statistic for this hypothesis -> {\"coverage_note\": \"counts are over the sampled users only; the coverage is the number of users and items the probe read\", \"distinct_edges\": 115582, \"edge_density\": 5.3266, \"edges\": 118315, \"mean_outgoing_degree\": 5.4526,\n  [E11] OK | measured train-only statistic for this hypothesis -> {\"note\": \"a diagnostic about the existing baseline SIDs; never an admission gate\", \"permuted_null_same_first_prefix_rate\": 0.067, \"same_first_prefix_rate\": 0.0907, \"source\": \"results/stage2_RQ-VAE/TIGER_RQ-VAE/item_sids.\n\nGEOMETRIC_NECESSITY:\n  [E12] PROPOSED | the curved operation -> Poincaré ball distance with Möbius addition and a per-pair negative sectional curvature -c_ik, where c_ik = c_l*exp(-a_ik) and c_l = clamp(exp(-delta_l/2), 0.25, 4.0) with c_0 = 1 dimensionless: d_c(u,v) = (2/sqrt(c))*ar\n  [E13] PROPOSED | where it acts -> Inside the residual quantizer's assignment step at all three levels, and in the gradient that flows through the straight-through soft plan to the encoder and\n\n### CURVCHART-EQUIMARGIN-RQ\nEVIDENCE BUNDLE 634a0d7731a5d022\nrubric rank-2026-10-v1\n\nBEHAVIORAL_EVIDENCE:\n  [E1] PROPOSED | the proposed training-only signal -> Directed item transitions (u -> v, v the next interaction in the same training sequence), aggregated into a code-level transition graph; the quantity the mechanism consumes is the Ollivier curvature of that quotient grap\n  [E2] PROPOSED | how it is computed -> Enumerated from TRAINING split interactions only, in order, giving a multiset `T_train` of directed pairs (u,v). For each level l each pair is mapped to `(A_l[u], A_l[v])` using the last-synced detached memberships, EMA-\n  [E3] PROPOSED | why it cannot leak -> The transition set is built exclusively from training-split sequences. Validation and test sequences are never enumerated, never mapped to codes, never enter the quotient graph or the null. The null shuffles only trainin\n  [E4] OBSERVED | the frozen training data contract\n  [E5] OBSERVED | measured successor-entropy stratification on the train split: top-1 successor mass 0.4375 in the lowest entropy quintile against 0.0543 in the highest, Spearman(entropy, top-1 mass) = -0.9732738648557935; bin 1 H=0.931 support 2.8 distinct 2.72 top1 0.438; bin 2 H=1.505 support 4.6 distinct 4.54 top1 0.227; bin 3 H=1.875 support 6.7 distinct 6.60 top1 0.162; bin 4 H=2.362 support 11.0 distinct 10.84 top1 0.106; bin 5 H=3.405 support 44.3 distinct 41.41 top1 0.054 -> {\"bins\": [{\"bin\": 1, \"entropy_range\": [-0.0, 1.3863], \"items\": 4895, \"mean_distinct_successors\": 2.723, \"mean_entropy\": 0.931, \"mean_support\": 2.77, \"mean_top1_mass\": 0.4375, \"mean_unique_ratio\": 0.9899}, {\"bin\": 2, \"ent\n  [E6] OBSERVED | measured width-20 beam survival on the 57,439-row test split: l1_br: recall@10 0.04671, target SID inside the 20 beams 0.0678, gold prefix alive at depth 1/2/3/4 1.000/1.000/1.000/0.068; l1_br_euclid: recall@10 0.06207, target SID inside the 20 beams 0.0847, gold prefix alive at depth 1/2/3/4 1.000/0.829/0.161/0.085; l1_only: recall@10 0.06233, target SID inside the 20 beams 0.0855, gold prefix alive at depth 1/2/3/4 1.000/0.829/0.156/0.086; resample: recall@10 0.06363, target SID inside the 20 beams 0.0884, gold prefix alive at depth 1/2/3/4 0.497/0.122/0.091/0.088; successor_entropy: recall@10 0.05122, target SID inside the 20 beams 0.0688, gold prefix alive at depth 1/2/3/4 0.735/0.400/0.133/0.069; successor_geodesic_coarse: recall@10 0.05500, target SID inside the 20 beams 0.0740, gold prefix alive at depth 1/2/3/4 0.989/0.341/0.122/0.074; successor_geodesic_coarse_v2: recall@10 0.05463, target SID inside the 20 beams 0.0736, gold prefix alive at depth 1/2/3/4 0.995/0.388/0.135/0.074; tangent_successor_residual: recall@10 0.05500, target SID inside the 20 beams 0.0731, gold prefix alive at depth 1/2/3/4 0.643/0.180/0.090/0.073 -> {\"l1_br\": {\"beam\": {\"beam_width\": 20, \"categories\": {\"hit_from_beams\": 2683, \"sid_absent_from_beams\": 53546, \"sid_generated_dropped_before_top10\": 1210}, \"category_share\": {\"hit_from_beams\": 0.046710423231602224, \"sid_ab\n  [E7] OBSERVED | measured teacher-forced per-position NLL: l1_br: T1/T2/T3/T4 NLL 0.00/0.00/0.00/9.03; l1_br_euclid: T1/T2/T3/T4 NLL 0.00/3.22/4.36/1.23; l1_only: T1/T2/T3/T4 NLL 0.00/3.23/4.38/1.19; resample: T1/T2/T3/T4 N